# PeaBrain MCP server identity (canonical, fixed): user and group
# peabrain, UID/GID 181. First free ID above the highest claimed
# identity (180 lpadmin) - verified against accounts.tsv and every
# tree-wide fragment; never reuse it for another identity.
#
# The binary itself is deliberately NOT setuid; privilege
# transition happens through the packaged sudoers fragment
# (files/sudoers.d/peabrain): a setuid transition blinds the
# process's own /proc/self/environ reads (verified on Egg), while
# a full user switch via sudo carries a complete environment.
#
# State dir /var/saphira/PeaBrain is 0700: the binary refuses to run
# against any state directory that is not 0700 and owner-only
# (proven on Egg), so the declaration matches the enforcement.
user peabrain 181 peabrain /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group peabrain 181
dir /var/saphira/PeaBrain 0700 peabrain peabrain
